2.3. Kernel‑Specific Representations of the Invariant Family

Each invariant \(I_j \in \mathcal{I}\) is represented differently in each kernel:

\[
\rho{phys}(Ij), \qquad \rho{lat}(Ij), \qquad \rho{id}(Ij).
\]

Examples include:

- Energy: \(\hat{H}, \epsilon(k), \mathcal{E}[\Psi]\)  
- Symmetry: \(\hat{I}{phys}, Rg, \hat{M}\)  
- Momentum: \(\hat{P}, T{pn}, \partial_x \Psi\)

These representations form operator families:

\[
\mathcal{O}j = \{\rho{phys}(Ij), \rho{lat}(Ij), \rho{id}(I_j)\}.
\]

Each family is structurally identical across kernels, differing only in operator realization.

