2.4. Hamiltonian Realization of SUFT

The SUFT structural law is extended into a Hamiltonian form:

\[
\hat{H}_{total}
=
\hat{H}_{phys}
+
\hat{H}_{lat}
+
\hat{H}_{id},
\]

with each kernel contributing:

\[
\hat{H}X = \sumj \lambdaj^{(X)} \rhoX(I_j).
\]

The identity field \(\Psi\) evolves according to:

\[
\frac{\partial \Psi}{\partial t}
=
-i \frac{\partial}{\partial \Psi^\dagger}
\hat{H}_{total}.
\]

This is the first dynamical equation in the SUFT lineage, generalizing Hamiltonian mechanics to include coherence and identity as conserved structural quantities.

